{"id": "q013", "type": "multi_hop", "question": "My agent runs on a different machine than the server. Which address does it connect to, and how do server and agent prove they trust each other?", "answer": "The agent connects to the server using the address specified in the `WOODPECKER_SERVER` environment variable. In the given context, the server address is set to `woodpecker-server:9000`. The server and agent prove they trust each other using a shared secret, which is configured via the `WOODPECKER_AGENT_SECRET` environment variable. Both the server and agent need to have the same secret to authenticate their communication. [1][2][3]", "abstained": false, "abstain_reason": null, "sources": [{"n": 1, "chunk_id": "efeb9bd5c9cf:header:2", "source": "30-administration/05-installation/10-docker-compose.md", "section": "Docker Compose", "score": 0.016009221311475412}, {"n": 2, "chunk_id": "4e46e906332a:header:2", "source": "30-administration/10-configuration/30-agent.md", "section": "Agent > Agent registration", "score": 0.01575682382133995}, {"n": 3, "chunk_id": "4e46e906332a:header:3", "source": "30-administration/10-configuration/30-agent.md", "section": "Agent > Agent registration > Using system token", "score": 0.014938684503901897}, {"n": 4, "chunk_id": "735989d3cd01:header:6", "source": "92-development/05-architecture.md", "section": "Architecture > System architecture > Agent", "score": 0.014925373134328358}, {"n": 5, "chunk_id": "4e46e906332a:header:0", "source": "30-administration/10-configuration/30-agent.md", "section": "Agent", "score": 0.00819672131147541}], "verification": {"verdicts": [{"claim_index": 3, "passage": 1, "supported": true, "judge_missing": false}, {"claim_index": 3, "passage": 2, "supported": true, "judge_missing": false}, {"claim_index": 3, "passage": 3, "supported": true, "judge_missing": false}], "citation_precision": 1.0, "claim_coverage": 0.25, "uncited_claims": 3, "invalid_citations": 0}, "timings": {"retrieval_s": 0.033, "generation_